<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petronilla of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1136–<a href="/years/1173">1173</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Petronila of Aragon · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimenez-dynasty">Jiménez dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petronilla was queen of Aragon from 1137 to 1164, the daughter and heiress of Ramiro II. Betrothed as an infant in 1137 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona</a>, who then governed Aragon, she married him in 1150. The union joined Aragon and the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in what became the Crown of Aragon, and in 1164 she abdicated in favour of their son Alfonso II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petronilla-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Petronilla of Aragon" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Escarlati; Genealogía anónima por iniciativa de Martín I de Aragón, &quot;El Humano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peronella_reina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His daughter <b>Petronila</b> was betrothed in 1137, when still an infant, to Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona, who governed Aragon as its prince while keeping his own counties.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Ramiro II, a monk called from the cloister to the throne in 1134, married to provide an heir and retired to monastic life once his baby daughter <b>Petronila</b> was betrothed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>His marriage to <b>Petronila</b>, heiress of the Kingdom of Aragon, agreed in 1137, joined the two dynasties, and in 1162 their son Alfonso II inherited Barcelona and soon Aragon, so that the Catalan counties became one constituent of the Crown of Aragon.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1137 Ramon Berenguer IV was betrothed to <b>Petronilla</b>, heiress of Aragon, and governed both lands.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-barcelona">County of Barcelona</a></li></ul></section>
